---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Shot from '../../components/Shot.astro';
import Num from '../../components/Num.astro';
import panel from '../../assets/pr-dist-r/panel.webp';

// The plugin's view at its default size, 630 × 890: the pedal y 0–850 (6 px a millimetre), the
// bottom bar y 850–890. The top bar is the host's, above it, and isn't in the shot.
const base = { w: 630, h: 890 };
// A box in panel millimetres (machines/rat/docs/panel.json) as view pixels; the front face is
// drawn under the top, foreshortened to 0.42.
const ox = 6.008, oy = 9;
const mm = (x0: number, y0: number, x1: number, y1: number) => ({ x: (x0 + ox) * 6, y: (y0 + oy) * 6, w: (x1 - x0) * 6, h: (y1 - y0) * 6 });
const front = (x0: number, z0: number, x1: number, z1: number) => mm(x0, 102.13 + z0 * 0.42, x1, 102.13 + z1 * 0.42);
const at = {
  model: mm(33.21, 54.15, 77.87, 65.25),
  maker: mm(16.82, 53.57, 30.2, 65.09),
  front: front(31.5, 13.19, 61.61, 37.53),
  dist: mm(10.96, 21.45, 29.02, 39.51),
  filter: mm(37.92, 21.51, 55.98, 39.57),
  volume: mm(64.78, 21.47, 82.84, 39.53),
  foot: mm(37.26, 75.28, 54.14, 92.16),
  input: { x: 10, y: 857, w: 150, h: 26 },
};

// The sections and their headings, for the contents at the top and the sidebar. Keep in step
// with the ids and headings below.
type Entry = { id: string; title: string; sub?: Entry[] };
const toc: Entry[] = [
  { id: 'start', title: 'Getting started', sub: [
    { id: 'first-start', title: 'The first start' },
    { id: 'artwork', title: 'Panel artwork' },
  ] },
  { id: 'pedal', title: 'The pedal', sub: [
    { id: 'knobs', title: 'The knobs' },
    { id: 'footswitch', title: 'The footswitch' },
  ] },
  { id: 'bars', title: 'The bars', sub: [
    { id: 'top-bar', title: 'The top bar' },
    { id: 'state', title: 'State' },
    { id: 'bottom-bar', title: 'The bottom bar' },
  ] },
  { id: 'daw', title: 'Your DAW', sub: [
    { id: 'drive', title: 'Driving it' },
    { id: 'automation', title: 'Automation and sessions' },
  ] },
  { id: 'keyboard', title: 'Keyboard and mouse' },
];
---
<Base title="pr-dist-r user guide · Lemus" description="How to use pr-dist-r: panel artwork, the knobs and the footswitch, INPUT, driving it from your DAW, automation and sessions." current="pr-dist-r">

<div class="sheet">
<div class="col guide">

<!-- Beside the guide on a wide window; on a narrow one, a drawer behind the Contents button. -->
<nav class="side" id="contents" aria-label="Contents">
<div class="label">Contents</div>
<ol>
{toc.map((s, i) => (
<li>
<a href={`#${s.id}`} class="top"><span class="n">{i + 1}</span>{s.title}</a>
{s.sub && <ol>
{s.sub.map((h) => (
<li>
<a href={`#${h.id}`}>{h.title}</a>
{h.sub && <ol>{h.sub.map((g) => <li><a href={`#${g.id}`} class="deep">{g.title}</a></li>)}</ol>}
</li>
))}
</ol>}
</li>
))}
</ol>
</nav>
<button type="button" class="toc-button" aria-controls="contents" aria-expanded="false" hidden>
<svg aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M2 4h12M2 8h12M2 12h8"></path></svg>
<span>Contents</span>
</button>

<div class="main">
<header class="intro">
<nav aria-label="Breadcrumb" class="crumbs"><a href="/pr-dist-r">pr-dist-r</a> / User guide</nav>
<h1><span class="nowrap">pr-dist-r</span> user guide</h1>
<p class="lede">pr-dist-r is the original ProCo RAT, the 1984 small box: three knobs and a footswitch, and what you know from a RAT applies. This guide covers what the plugin adds. Installing is on the <a href="/download#installing">download page</a>; the ROM folder, artwork files, the update check and contact are on <a href="/support">Support</a>.</p>
<ol class="toc">
{toc.map(({ id, title }) => <li><a href={`#${id}`}>{title}</a></li>)}
</ol>
</header>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="start">
<div class="eyebrow">1</div>
<h2>Getting started</h2>

<h3 id="first-start">The first start</h3>
<p>pr-dist-r is a circuit with no firmware, so it needs no ROM. It's an effect: insert it on a track or bus, and it's on.</p>

<h3 id="artwork">Panel artwork</h3>
<p>The three blank places take an SVG or PNG of your own each, named as below, anywhere in the ROM folder (<a href="/support#artwork">how artwork files work</a>). <span class="k">ROMs</span> in the top bar lists them with what each has, opens the folder with Show its folder, and reads it again with Rescan.</p>
<div class="narrow"><Shot src={panel} base={base} alt="The pedal with the three blank artwork places outlined: the RAT letters and the Pro Co logo in the white block, and the logo on the front face" crop={{ x: 40, y: 330, w: 550, h: 470 }} marks={[{ ...at.model, n: 'model' }, { ...at.maker, n: 'maker' }, { ...at.front, n: 'front' }]} caption="The three places. The front face is drawn under the top, foreshortened." /></div>
<div class="scroll">
<table>
<thead><tr><th scope="col">File</th><th scope="col">Place</th><th scope="col">Size</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td class="mono">pr-dist-r-model.svg or .png</td><td>The RAT letters, black in the white block</td><td>44.7 × 11.1 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">pr-dist-r-maker.svg or .png</td><td>The Pro Co logo beside them</td><td>13.4 × 11.5 mm</td></tr>
<tr><td class="mono">pr-dist-r-front.svg or .png</td><td>The Pro Co Sound Inc logo on the front face</td><td>30.1 × 24.3 mm</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p>The plain names (<span class="mono">model.svg</span>…) in <span class="path">artwork/rat/</span> or <span class="mono">artwork/rat.zip</span> work too, and win over these. Without them the white block is plain.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="pedal">
<div class="eyebrow">2</div>
<h2>The pedal</h2>
<p>The top of the 1984 small box, measured from photos of 1984 units.</p>
<div class="narrow"><Shot src={panel} base={base} alt="DISTORTION, FILTER and VOLUME and the footswitch outlined" crop={{ x: 40, y: 100, w: 550, h: 520 }} marks={[{ ...at.dist, n: 1 }, { ...at.filter, n: 2 }, { ...at.volume, n: 3 }, { ...at.foot, n: 4 }]} /></div>

<h3 id="knobs">The knobs</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">DISTORTION</span> <Num n="1" />: the gain before the clipping diodes.</li>
<li><span class="k">FILTER</span> <Num n="2" />: a low-pass after them. Clockwise is darker.</li>
<li><span class="k">VOLUME</span> <Num n="3" />: the output level.</li>
</ul>
<p>Each reads 0 to 10 in the DAW and on its tooltip; the pedal's scale has seven ticks. A new instance has them at 5, 4 and 5.</p>

<h3 id="footswitch">The footswitch</h3>
<p><Num n="4" /> True bypass: off, the track passes through untouched, INPUT included. The 1984 RAT has no LED, so the bottom bar says ON or BYPASSED. Switching crossfades over 5 ms instead of the real switch's click.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="bars">
<div class="eyebrow">3</div>
<h2>The bars</h2>

<h3 id="top-bar">The top bar</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">BETA</span> after the name: this version is a beta. About shows the version.</li>
<li><span class="k">ROMs:</span> the ROM folder and the <a href="#artwork">artwork</a>, with their full paths, and Show, Change… and Rescan for the folder.</li>
<li><span class="k">State:</span> see <a href="#state">State</a>.</li>
<li><span class="k">About:</span> the version, the ROM folder and artwork in use, the <a href="/support#updates">update check</a>, and links to this guide, the site and the forum. A newer version shows as a button in the bar.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="state">State</h3>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Save to file…</span> saves the instance: the knobs, the footswitch and INPUT.</li>
<li><span class="k">Load from file…</span> loads one.</li>
<li><span class="k">Reset…</span> makes it a new instance: every control at its default.</li>
</ul>

<h3 id="bottom-bar">The bottom bar</h3>
<Shot src={panel} base={base} alt="The bottom bar: INPUT, the status and ?" crop={{ x: 0, y: 830, w: 630, h: 60 }} marks={[{ ...at.input, n: 1 }]} />
<dl class="legend">
<div><dt>INPUT <Num n="1" /></dt><dd>A gain in front of the pedal, −12 to +24 dB, default 0 dB, to hit it harder or softer. At 0 dB, 0 dBFS is +4 dBu at the pedal's input (1.74 V peak), about a hot humbucker or a synth's line output. The output isn't made up for it. Drag it sideways or scroll; double-click goes back to 0 dB.</dd></div>
<div><dt>ON, BYPASSED</dt><dd>The footswitch, and while a knob is turned, its value.</dd></div>
<div><dt>?</dt><dd>Shows the list of computer keys over the pedal. Any click, ? or Escape closes it.</dd></div>
</dl>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="daw">
<div class="eyebrow">4</div>
<h2>Your DAW</h2>
<p>An effect, mono or stereo: on a stereo track each side has its own pedal, and a mono source played on both sides costs one.</p>

<h3 id="drive">Driving it</h3>
<p>A RAT reacts to how hot its input is. In most DAWs the fader comes after the plugin, so it doesn't change that: INPUT does, as do clip gain, a gain plugin before it, or the source's own volume.</p>

<h3 id="automation">Automation and sessions</h3>
<p>Five parameters can be automated, in this order: Distortion, Filter, Volume, On, Input. Knob moves glide over a few milliseconds, as a turned pot does.</p>
<p>A session saves them, as <a href="#state">State</a> does, with the version of the model it was made with.</p>
<p>On silent input the pedal sleeps and puts out exact zeros; any sound or knob move wakes it. pr-dist-r reports a 1 s tail.</p>
</section>

<!-- ===================================================================== -->
<section id="keyboard">
<div class="eyebrow">5</div>
<h2>Keyboard and mouse</h2>
<ul>
<li><span class="k">Knobs:</span> drag up or down, or scroll; shift is finer, double-click goes back to the default. Hovering shows the value.</li>
<li><span class="k">Footswitch:</span> click.</li>
<li><span class="k">?</span> shows the key list; <span class="k">Escape</span> closes it. Click the pedal first.</li>
<li><span class="k">Window:</span> drag the bottom-right corner, half to twice the size.</li>
</ul>
</section>

</div>

</div>
</div>

</Base>

<script>
// The sidebar marks the heading being read and opens its section; the button opens it as a
// drawer on a narrow window. Without this script the sidebar shows every heading.
const nav = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('.side')!;
const button = document.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('.toc-button')!;
const links = [...nav.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('a')];
const targets = links.map((a) => document.getElementById(a.hash.slice(1))!);
nav.classList.add('spy');
button.hidden = false;

let current = -1;
function mark() {
  let i = -1;
  targets.forEach((t, j) => { if (t.getBoundingClientRect().top <= 120) i = j; });
  // At the end of the page the last headings can't reach the top: take the one jumped to, if
  // it's in view, or else the last.
  if (innerHeight + scrollY >= document.documentElement.scrollHeight - 2) {
    const jumped = targets.findIndex((t) => '#' + t.id === location.hash);
    i = jumped >= 0 && targets[jumped].getBoundingClientRect().top < innerHeight ? jumped : targets.length - 1;
  }
  if (i === current) return;
  current = i;
  links.forEach((a, j) => {
    a.classList.toggle('on', j === i);
    if (j === i) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'location'); else a.removeAttribute('aria-current');
  });
  const section = i >= 0 ? links[i].closest('.side > ol > li') : null;
  for (const li of nav.querySelectorAll(':scope > ol > li')) li.classList.toggle('open', li === section);
  reveal();
}

// Keep the marked heading in view when the sidebar is taller than the window.
function reveal() {
  const a = links[current];
  if (!a || nav.scrollHeight <= nav.clientHeight) return;
  if (a.offsetTop < nav.scrollTop || a.offsetTop + a.offsetHeight > nav.scrollTop + nav.clientHeight)
    nav.scrollTop = a.offsetTop - nav.clientHeight / 3;
}

let frame = 0;
const later = () => { if (!frame) frame = requestAnimationFrame(() => { frame = 0; mark(); }); };
addEventListener('scroll', later, { passive: true });
addEventListener('resize', later);
addEventListener('hashchange', later);
mark();

function open(on: boolean) {
  nav.classList.toggle('open', on);
  button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(on));
  button.querySelector('span')!.textContent = on ? 'Close' : 'Contents';
  if (on) reveal();
}
button.addEventListener('click', () => open(!nav.classList.contains('open')));
nav.addEventListener('click', (e) => { if ((e.target as Element).closest('a')) open(false); });
document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  if (nav.classList.contains('open') && !nav.contains(e.target as Node) && !button.contains(e.target as Node)) open(false);
});
document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
  if (e.key === 'Escape' && nav.classList.contains('open')) { open(false); button.focus(); }
});
</script>

<style>
.guide { padding-bottom: 96px; }
.narrow { max-width: 560px; }
.main { min-width: 0; max-width: 1000px; }

.side { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.45; }
.side .label { padding: 0 0 10px 12px; }
.side ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0; max-width: none; }
.side li { font-size: inherit; color: inherit; }
.side > ol > li + li { margin-top: 6px; }
.side a { display: flex; gap: 8px; padding: 3px 10px 3px 30px; border-left: 2px solid var(--rule); color: var(--ink2); text-decoration: none; }
.side a.top { padding-left: 10px; color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.side a.deep { padding-left: 44px; }
.side .n { flex: 0 0 auto; min-width: 12px; font: 12px/1.7 var(--mono); color: var(--ink3); }
.side a:hover { color: var(--ink); border-left-color: var(--ink2); }
.side a.on { color: var(--wire-text); border-left-color: var(--wire); }
.side a.on .n { color: var(--wire-text); }
.toc-button { display: none; }

@media (min-width: 1080px) {
  .guide { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 236px minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 56px; }
  .side { position: sticky; top: 0; align-self: start; max-height: 100vh; overflow-y: auto; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 56px 0 32px; scrollbar-width: thin; }
  .side.spy > ol > li:not(.open) > ol { display: none; }
  .intro .toc { display: none; }
}
@media (max-width: 1079.98px) {
  .side { display: none; }
  .side.open { display: block; position: fixed; top: 0; bottom: 0; left: 0; z-index: 20; width: min(320px, 85vw); box-sizing: border-box; overflow-y: auto; padding: 24px 16px 96px; background: var(--paper); border-right: 2px solid var(--ink); box-shadow: 0 0 0 100vmax rgba(22, 26, 38, 0.45); }
  .toc-button:not([hidden]) { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; position: fixed; left: 16px; bottom: 16px; z-index: 21; min-height: 44px; padding: 0 18px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 2px solid var(--ink); border-radius: 0; background: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); font-family: var(--display); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; cursor: pointer; box-shadow: 0 6px 20px rgba(22, 26, 38, 0.25); }
  .toc-button:hover { background: var(--wire-text); border-color: var(--wire-text); }
}
.intro { padding: 56px 0 24px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; }
.crumbs { font-size: 14px; color: var(--ink2); }
h1 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(40px, 5.4vw, 68px); line-height: 0.95; }
.lede { margin: 0; color: var(--ink2); font-size: 18px; max-width: 44em; }
.nowrap { white-space: nowrap; }
.toc { margin: 8px 0 0; padding: 16px 20px 16px 44px; border: 2px solid var(--ink); display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(min(100%, 260px), 1fr)); gap: 4px 24px; color: var(--ink3); }
section { padding: 48px 0 8px; border-top: 1.5px solid var(--ink); margin-top: 32px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
.eyebrow { width: 44px; height: 44px; box-sizing: border-box; border: 2px solid var(--ink); display: grid; place-items: center; font: 700 16px var(--mono); }
h2 { margin: 0; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 700; font-size: clamp(32px, 3.8vw, 44px); line-height: 1; text-transform: uppercase; }
h3 { margin: 20px 0 0; font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 25px; line-height: 1.15; letter-spacing: 0.02em; text-transform: uppercase; scroll-margin-top: 16px; }
p, li, dd { color: var(--ink2); font-size: 16px; }
p { margin: 0; max-width: 46em; }
ul, ol { margin: 0; padding-left: 22px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; max-width: 46em; }
.k { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
.mono { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--ink); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
td.mono { white-space: nowrap; overflow-wrap: normal; }
.path { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 0.88em; color: var(--ink); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
.card { border: 2px solid var(--ink); padding: 18px 20px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; max-width: 46em; }
.label { font-family: var(--display); font-size: 13px; letter-spacing: 0.1em; font-weight: 600; color: var(--ink2); text-transform: uppercase; }
.scroll { overflow-x: auto; border: 2px solid var(--ink); }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 15px; min-width: 520px; }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 10px 16px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule); vertical-align: top; color: var(--ink2); }
thead th { background: var(--paper2); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); font-family: var(--display); font-weight: 600; font-size: 15px; letter-spacing: 0.08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink); }
tbody th { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
tbody tr:last-child th, tbody tr:last-child td { border-bottom: 0; }
.legend { margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 12px; max-width: 52em; }
.legend dt { color: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; font-size: 16px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
.legend dd { margin: 2px 0 0; }
</style>
